  <prompt>Execute a REAL end-to-end customer provisioning run against a dev Model-2-Spaarke-hosted stamp using the NOW-FUNCTIONAL pipeline (every handler real per Waves G-1..G-7, dispatcher live, H13's real aggregation gate wired per task 185): invoke the run via the `/provision-environment` skill (this project's Phase D deliverable, already ✅) or a direct L2 REST call; poll the run to completion across the 24h SPE replication gate + any consent-latency gates; verify sprk_dataverseenvironment.SetupStatus REACHES Ready (task 184's real writer, gated by task 185's real aggregation) -- for the FIRST TIME via actual code execution, not a claimed/simulated pass. This supersedes the original task 089 (Phase F, currently SPLIT MODE per TASK-INDEX.md — scaffolding landed, owner invocation pending) by actually exercising the pipeline this whole Phase C'' build exists to make real.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer / provisioning operator. Expert in coordinating a full multi-day E2E acceptance run, monitoring dispatcher/reconciler health across a live run, and escalating per this project's Human Escalation Triggers if any gate misbehaves.</role>

  <goal>A real customer provisioning run reaches sprk_dataverseenvironment.SetupStatus = Ready via the fully-real pipeline. All 6 T1-T6 traps and all 5 I1-I5 invariants are confirmed Pass by task 185's real aggregation (not fakes). The naming-conformance and cost-envelope checks Pass. A comprehensive acceptance report is filed superseding the prior scaffolding-only Phase F report, documenting: total wall-clock (compared against DS-2b's ~26-28h estimate), any manual-gate latencies observed (H0.5 admin consent, H8's 24h SPE gate, H11's B2B consent if applicable), and confirmation that this is the FIRST TIME the project's stated goal (FR-18/SC#5: E2E customer provisioning) has been demonstrated by actual code execution.</goal>

