  <escalation>
    <trigger name="pre-live-fire-punch-list-gate" added-by="task 202" date="2026-08-24">**PRE-CHECK GATE (BINDING per owner directive 2026-08-24 SESSION 5)** — Before invoking `/provision-environment`, READ `projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/task-202-punch-list.md`. If ANY Class-A row with `blocks_e2e=yes` has `last_known_status != applied` (i.e. task 203 has not landed it) OR ANY Class-B row with `blocks_e2e=yes` has not been merged from its target BFF-owning worktree (`code-quality-and-assurance-r3` or successor), ABORT this task and defer to task 203 + BFF-worktree coordination. Reason: task 186 E2E ceremony's purpose is to PROVE the customer-provisioning platform works end-to-end, not to iterate through fail-cycles for known-unapplied lessons. The punch list header lists 26 Class-A + 12 Class-B `blocks_e2e=yes` rows that MUST all be `applied` before this task fires. Verification query (task 186 executor): `grep -c "last_known_status: applied" notes/task-202-punch-list.md` should match count of `blocks_e2e: yes` rows. If ambiguous, escalate to owner rather than proceeding on assumption.</trigger>
    <trigger>If ANY of the 6 T1-T6 traps, 5 I1-I5 invariants, naming-conformance, or cost-envelope checks FAILS during this run, STOP and escalate per this project's Human Escalation Triggers — do NOT mark the run as accepted with a documented exception; a Wave G-7 acceptance-gate failure on the FIRST real run is exactly the signal the entire Phase C'' build exists to surface honestly, and papering over it here would recreate the original overstatement problem DS-4's audit found.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the run's wall-clock materially exceeds DS-2b's ~26-28h estimate (excluding the known 24h SPE gate) by a wide margin, STOP and escalate to determine whether a specific handler is pathologically slow (a correctness-adjacent regression, not merely a performance curiosity) rather than silently absorbing the delay.</trigger>
