  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">sprk_dataverseenvironment.SetupStatus reaches Ready for the run's target customer, verified by an independent Dataverse read (not merely the run's own self-report).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All 6 T1-T6 traps report Pass (verified via the run's logs/report, sourced from task 185's real aggregation, not a fake).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All 5 I1-I5 invariants report Pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">naming-conformance and cost-envelope checks report Pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">/health succeeds; sample analysis + sample doc upload+index + workspace-layout render + wizard field-map all succeed per IE2EValidationRunner's real checks (task 181).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A comprehensive acceptance report exists documenting wall-clock, gate latencies, and any deviations, explicitly confirming this is the first genuine (non-scaffolding) E2E demonstration of FR-18/SC#5.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true" added-by="task 202 A40" date="2026-08-25">**T1 site-property post-condition (auth-v4 §10.1 Δ4 + FR-37)** — After H4 completes AND after BFF App Service deployment (H9), the runner MUST assert `keyVaultReferenceIdentity` is set to the BFF runtime UAMI's resource ID on BOTH the production slot AND the staging slot. Assertions:
      - `az webapp show --name {app} --resource-group {rg} --query "keyVaultReferenceIdentity" -o tsv` MUST equal the exact UAMI resource ID (case-sensitive full ARM path — NOT `SystemAssigned`, NOT empty, NOT `null`).
      - `az webapp show --name {app} --resource-group {rg} --slot staging --query "keyVaultReferenceIdentity" -o tsv` MUST equal the SAME UAMI resource ID (T5 slot-parity per spec.md FR-33).
      - If either assertion fails: acceptance run MUST fail with rejection code equivalent to `TrapT1VerificationMismatch` and diagnostic literal "T1 trap tripped — site would SIGABRT (exit 134) on first `@Microsoft.KeyVault(...)` app-setting resolution attempt; provisioning claimed T1-cleared but post-deployment site property does not match — escalate per Human Escalation Triggers (§6)". Do NOT accept the run under a documented exception — a Wave G-7 T1 regression on the FIRST real run is exactly the signal Phase C'' exists to surface honestly.
      - Rationale: `keyVaultReferenceIdentity` is a SITE property, not an app setting, and is NOT copied by `az webapp deployment slot create --configuration-source` (auth-v4 §10.2). If H9 (or any rollback ceremony per obligation 051-E) created a new slot without re-asserting the property, the H4→H9 slot-parity guarantee is broken and the new slot will SIGABRT on first startup even though H4's own probe (`IArmKeyVaultRefProbe`, task 044/123) reported PASS at H4-completion time.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Justification (CLAUDE.md §11): Existing -- the ORIGINAL task 089 scaffolding (harness + report skeleton + operator runbook) already exists and is reused, not rebuilt. Extension -- this task is the genuine EXECUTION the scaffolding was always meant to support, now that the pipeline underneath it is real. Cost-of-doing-nothing -- without this task, the project's stated goal (E2E customer provisioning per FR-18/SC#5) remains UNDEMONSTRATED even after every Wave G-1..G-7 fix lands individually — this is the task that actually closes the loop the r1-gap-analysis opened.</notes>

